    ['Mirror of life trapping', 'magic', 50, '200000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This crystal mirror, about 4 feet square, is activated and deactivated by a command word. It has fifteen extradimensional cells. Any creature within 30 feet that sees its reflection must make a DC 23 Will save or be trapped bodily in a cell, its equipment left behind; a creature that knows what the mirror does and avoids looking has a 50 percent chance of seeing it (as a gaze attack). Constructs, undead and objects aren’t trapped. With the right command words, the owner can call a prisoner’s reflection to the surface to talk with it, or free it. When the mirror is full, a new prisoner frees one at random; breaking it frees them all. Strong abjuration; CL 17th.'],
    ['Mirror of mental prowess', 'magic', 40, '175000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This mirror, 5 feet tall and 2 feet wide, does the following for an owner who knows its commands: read the thoughts of any creature reflected in it while the owner is within 25 feet, even in an unknown language; view other places as with clairvoyance, even other planes the viewer knows well; serve as a portal to a place so viewed, which others can follow her through, leaving an invisible portal back that closes when she returns, by command, or after 24 hours, trapping her (creatures of Intelligence 12 or higher may notice it); and once a week answer one short question about a creature shown on it, as legend lore. Strong conjuration and divination; CL 17th.'],
    ['Mirror of opposition', 'magic', 45, '92000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This item resembles a normal mirror about 4 feet long and 3 feet wide. It can be hung or placed on a surface and then activated by speaking a command word. The same command word deactivates the mirror. If a creature sees its reflection in the mirror’s surface, an exact duplicate of that creature comes into being. This opposite immediately attacks the original. The duplicate has all the possessions and powers of its original (including magic). Upon the defeat or destruction of either the duplicate or the original, the duplicate and her items disappear completely. The mirror functions up to four times per day. Strong necromancy; CL 15th.'],
    ['Mithral full plate of speed', 'magic', 0, '26500 gp', ['armor', 'major'], 'As a free action, the wearer of this fine set of +1 mithral full plate can activate it, enabling her to act as though affected by a haste spell for up to 10 rounds each day. The duration of the haste effect need not be consecutive rounds. Speed while wearing a suit of mithral full plate is 20 feet for Medium creatures, or 15 feet for Small. The armor has an arcane spell failure chance of 25%, a maximum Dexterity bonus of +3, and an armor check penalty of -3. It is considered medium armor and weighs 25 pounds. Faint transmutation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Mithral heavy shield', 'magic', 0, '1020 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'shield'], 'This heavy shield is made of mithral and thus is much lighter than a standard steel shield. It has a 5% arcane spell failure chance and no armor check penalty. It weighs 5 pounds. No aura (nonmagical).'],
    ['Mithral shirt', 'magic', 0, '1100 gp', ['armor', 'medium', 'minor'], 'This extremely light chain shirt is made of very fine mithral links. Speed while wearing a mithral shirt is 30 feet for Medium creatures, or 20 feet for Small. The armor has an arcane spell failure chance of 10%, a maximum Dexterity bonus of +6, and no armor check penalty. It is considered light armor and weighs 10 pounds. No aura (nonmagical).'],
    ['Necklace of adaptation', 'magic', 0, '9000 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This necklace is a heavy chain with a platinum medallion. The magic of the necklace wraps the wearer in a shell of fresh air, making him immune to all harmful vapors and gases (such as cloudkill and stinking cloud effects, as well as inhaled poisons) and allowing him to breathe, even underwater or in a vacuum. Moderate transmutation; CL 7th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type I', 'magic', 0, '1650 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type I necklace has one 5d6 sphere and two 3d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type II', 'magic', 0, '2700 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type II necklace has one 6d6 sphere, two 4d6 spheres and two 2d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type III', 'magic', 0, '4350 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type III necklace has one 7d6 sphere, two 5d6 spheres and four 3d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type IV', 'magic', 0, '5400 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type IV necklace has one 8d6 sphere, two 6d6 spheres, two 4d6 spheres and four 2d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type V', 'magic', 0, '6150 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type V necklace has one 9d6 sphere, two 7d6 spheres, two 5d6 spheres and two 3d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type VI', 'magic', 0, '8100 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type VI necklace has one 10d6 sphere, two 8d6 spheres, two 6d6 spheres and four 4d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Necklace of fireballs type VII', 'magic', 0, '9150 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This looks like beads on a string, but to whoever holds it, it is a golden chain hung with golden spheres (it doesn’t take up the neck slot). Only the wearer can detach a sphere, which is easily hurled up to 70 feet and detonates as a fireball (Reflex DC 14 half) of its own strength. A type VII necklace has one 10d6 sphere, two 9d6 spheres, two 7d6 spheres, two 5d6 spheres and two 3d6 spheres. If the wearer fails a save against a magical fire attack, the necklace must also save (+7), or all its spheres detonate at once. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Nine lives stealer', 'magic', 0, '23057 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'weapon'], 'This +2 longsword can draw the life force from an opponent nine times, then is a simple +2 longsword with a hint of evil. It works on a critical hit against a creature subject to critical hits, which must make a DC 20 Fortitude save or die; on a success, no use is spent and normal critical damage applies. The sword is evil: a good character wielding it gains two negative levels, which can’t be overcome while it is in hand and vanish when it isn’t, never causing actual level loss. Strong necromancy [evil]; CL 13th.'],
    ['Oathbow', 'magic', 0, '25600 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'weapon'], 'This white elven +2 composite longbow (+2 Str bonus) whispers in Elven when drawn. Once a day, if you swear aloud to slay a target (a free action), against that sworn enemy it has a +5 enhancement bonus, and its arrows deal an extra 2d6 damage and ×4 on a critical hit. Against all others it counts as only a masterwork weapon, and you take −1 on attacks with any other weapon. This lasts seven days or until you slay the enemy. You can have only one sworn enemy at a time, and can’t swear again for 24 hours after an oath, even if the enemy dies. Strong evocation; CL 15th.'],
