    ['Rapier of puncturing', 'magic', 0, '50320 gp', ['major', 'weapon'], 'Three times per day, this +2 wounding rapier allows the wielder to make a touch attack with the weapon that deals 1d6 points of Constitution damage by draining blood. Creatures immune to critical hits are immune to the Constitution damage dealt by this weapon. Strong necromancy; CL 13th.'],
    ['Restorative ointment', 'magic', 0.5, '4000 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'A jar of this unguent is 3 inches in diameter and 1 inch deep and contains five applications. Placed upon a poisoned wound or swallowed, the ointment detoxifies any poison (as neutralize poison). Applied to a diseased area, it removes disease (as remove disease). Rubbed on a wound, the ointment cures 1d8+5 points of damage (as cure light wounds). Faint conjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Rhino hide', 'magic', 0, '5165 gp', ['armor', 'medium'], 'This +2 hide armor is made from rhinoceros hide. In addition to granting a +2 enhancement bonus to AC, it has a -1 armor check penalty and deals an additional 2d6 points of damage on any successful charge attack made by the wearer, including a mounted charge. Moderate transmutation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Ring gates', 'magic', 1, '40000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'These come in pairs of iron rings about 18 inches across, which must be on the same plane and within 100 miles of each other. Whatever goes into one comes out of the other, up to 100 pounds a day (objects pushed partway and pulled back don’t count). You can reach, look, stab or cast a spell through; a Small character can slip through with a DC 13 Escape Artist check, and Tiny or smaller creatures pass easily. Each ring has a marked entry side and exit side. Strong conjuration; CL 17th.'],
    ['Ring of animal friendship', 'magic', 0, '10800 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'On command, this ring affects an animal as if the wearer had cast charm animal. Faint enchantment; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Ring of blinking', 'magic', 0, '27000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'On command, this ring makes the wearer blink, as with the blink spell. Moderate transmutation; CL 7th.'],
    ['Ring of chameleon power', 'magic', 0, '12700 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'As a free action, the wearer of this ring can gain the ability to magically blend in with the surroundings. This provides a +10 competence bonus on her Hide checks. As a standard action, she can also command the ring to utilize the spell disguise self as often as she wants. Faint illusion; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Ring of climbing', 'magic', 0, '2500 gp', ['minor', 'ring'], 'This ring is actually a magic leather cord that ties around a finger. It continually grants the wearer a +5 competence bonus on Climb checks. Faint transmutatation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of climbing, improved', 'magic', 0, '10000 gp', ['medium', 'ring'], 'As climbing, except it grants a +10 competence bonus on its wearer’s Climb checks. Faint transmutation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of counterspells', 'magic', 0, '4000 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'This ring might seem to be a ring of spell storing upon first examination. However, while it allows a single spell of 1st through 6th level to be cast into it, that spell cannot be cast out of the ring again. Instead, should that spell ever be cast upon the wearer, the spell is immediately countered, as a counterspell action, requiring no action (or even knowledge) on the wearer’s part. Once so used, the spell cast within the ring is gone. A new spell (or the same one as before) may be placed in it again. Moderate evocation; CL 11th.'],
    ['Ring of djinni calling', 'magic', 0, '125000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'One of the many rings of fable, this “genie” ring is most useful indeed. It serves as a special gate by means of which a specific djinni can be called from the Elemental Plane of Air. When the ring is rubbed (a standard action), the call goes out, and the djinni appears on the next round. The djinni faithfully obeys and serves the wearer of the ring, but never for more than 1 hour per day. If the djinni of the ring is ever killed, the ring becomes nonmagical and worthless. Strong conjuration; CL 17th.'],
    ['Ring of elemental command (air)', 'magic', 0, '200000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring looks like a ring of feather falling until fully activated by a special condition (such as single-handedly slaying an air elemental), and must be reactivated for each new wearer. Creatures of the Elemental Plane of Air can’t attack you or come within 5 feet (or you can instead try to charm one, as charm monster, Will DC 17, losing the protection if it fails). Such creatures take −1 on attacks against you; you get +2 on saves against their attacks, +4 morale on attacks against them, your weapons bypass their damage reduction, and you can converse with them. You take −2 on saves against earth-based effects. Powers: feather fall and resist energy (electricity) at will on yourself, wind wall at will, gust of wind twice a day, air walk on yourself once a day, chain lightning once a week. Strong conjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Ring of elemental command (earth)', 'magic', 0, '200000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring looks like a ring of meld into stone until fully activated by a special condition (such as single-handedly slaying an earth elemental), and must be reactivated for each new wearer. Creatures of the Elemental Plane of Earth can’t attack you or come within 5 feet (or you can instead try to charm one, as charm monster, Will DC 17, losing the protection if it fails). Such creatures take −1 on attacks against you; you get +2 on saves against their attacks, +4 morale on attacks against them, your weapons bypass their damage reduction, and you can converse with them. You take −2 on saves against air- or electricity-based effects. Powers: meld into stone at will on yourself, soften earth and stone at will, stone shape twice a day, wall of stone once a day, passwall twice a week, stoneskin on yourself once a week. Strong conjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Ring of elemental command (fire)', 'magic', 0, '200000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring looks like a major ring of energy resistance (fire) until fully activated by a special condition (such as single-handedly slaying an fire elemental), and must be reactivated for each new wearer. Creatures of the Elemental Plane of Fire can’t attack you or come within 5 feet (or you can instead try to charm one, as charm monster, Will DC 17, losing the protection if it fails). Such creatures take −1 on attacks against you; you get +2 on saves against their attacks, +4 morale on attacks against them, your weapons bypass their damage reduction, and you can converse with them. You take −2 on saves against water- or cold-based effects. Powers: resist energy (fire) as a major ring of energy resistance, burning hands at will, flaming sphere and pyrotechnics twice a day, wall of fire once a day, flame strike twice a week. Strong conjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Ring of elemental command (water)', 'magic', 0, '200000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring looks like a ring of water walking until fully activated by a special condition (such as single-handedly slaying an water elemental), and must be reactivated for each new wearer. Creatures of the Elemental Plane of Water can’t attack you or come within 5 feet (or you can instead try to charm one, as charm monster, Will DC 17, losing the protection if it fails). Such creatures take −1 on attacks against you; you get +2 on saves against their attacks, +4 morale on attacks against them, your weapons bypass their damage reduction, and you can converse with them. You take −2 on saves against fire-based effects. Powers: water walk, create water and water breathing at will, wall of ice once a day, ice storm and control water twice a week. Strong conjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Ring of energy resistance, greater', 'magic', 0, '44000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This reddish iron ring continually protects the wearer from damage from one type of energy—acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic (chosen by the creator of the item; determine randomly if found as part of a treasure hoard). Each time the wearer would normally take such damage, subtract the ring’s resistance value from the damage dealt. A minor ring of energy resistance grants 10 points of resistance. A major ring of energy resistance grants 20 points of resistance. A greater ring of energy resistance grants 30 points of resistance. Faint (minor or major) or moderate (greater) abjuration; CL 3rd (minor), 7th (major), or 11th (greater).'],
    ['Ring of energy resistance, major', 'magic', 0, '28000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'This reddish iron ring continually protects the wearer from damage from one type of energy—acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic (chosen by the creator of the item; determine randomly if found as part of a treasure hoard). Each time the wearer would normally take such damage, subtract the ring’s resistance value from the damage dealt. A minor ring of energy resistance grants 10 points of resistance. A major ring of energy resistance grants 20 points of resistance. A greater ring of energy resistance grants 30 points of resistance. Faint (minor or major) or moderate (greater) abjuration; CL 3rd (minor), 7th (major), or 11th (greater).'],
    ['Ring of energy resistance, minor', 'magic', 0, '12000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'This reddish iron ring continually protects the wearer from damage from one type of energy—acid, cold, electricity, fire, or sonic (chosen by the creator of the item; determine randomly if found as part of a treasure hoard). Each time the wearer would normally take such damage, subtract the ring’s resistance value from the damage dealt. A minor ring of energy resistance grants 10 points of resistance. A major ring of energy resistance grants 20 points of resistance. A greater ring of energy resistance grants 30 points of resistance. Faint (minor or major) or moderate (greater) abjuration; CL 3rd (minor), 7th (major), or 11th (greater).'],
    ['Ring of evasion', 'magic', 0, '25000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'This ring continually grants the wearer the ability to avoid damage as if she had evasion. Whenever she makes a Reflex saving throw to determine whether she takes half damage, a successful save results in no damage. Moderate transmutation; CL 7th.'],
    ['Ring of feather falling', 'magic', 0, '2200 gp', ['minor', 'ring'], 'This ring is crafted with a feather pattern all around its edge. It acts exactly like a feather fall spell, activated immediately if the wearer falls more than 5 feet. Faint transmutation; CL 1st.'],
    ['Ring of force shield', 'magic', 0, '8500 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'An iron band, this simple ring generates a shield-sized (and shield-shaped) wall of force that stays with the ring and can be wielded by the wearer as if it were a heavy shield (+2 AC). This special creation has no armor check penalty or arcane spell failure chance since it is weightless and encumbrance-free. It can be activated and deactivated at will as a free action. Moderate evocation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Ring of freedom of movement', 'magic', 0, '40000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This gold ring allows the wearer to act as if continually under the effect of a freedom of movement spell. Moderate abjuration; CL 7th.'],
    ['Ring of friend shield (pair)', 'magic', 0, '50000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'These curious rings always come in pairs. A friend shield ring without its mate is useless. Either wearer of one of a pair of the rings can, at any time, command his or her ring to cast a shield other spell with the wearer of the mated ring as the recipient. This effect has no range limitation. Moderate abjuration; CL 10th.'],
    ['Ring of invisibility', 'magic', 0, '20000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'By activating this simple silver ring, the wearer can benefit from invisibility, as the spell. Faint illusion; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Ring of jumping', 'magic', 0, '2500 gp', ['minor', 'ring'], 'This ring continually allows the wearer to leap about, providing a +5 competence bonus on all his Jump checks. Faint transmutation; CL 2nd.'],
    ['Ring of jumping, improved', 'magic', 0, '10000 gp', ['medium', 'ring'], 'As jumping, except it grants a +10 competence bonus on its wearer’s Jump check. Moderate transmutation; CL 7th.'],
    ['Ring of mind shielding', 'magic', 0, '8000 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'This ring is usually of fine workmanship and wrought from heavy gold. The wearer is continually immune to detect thoughts, discern lies, and any attempt to magically discern her alignment. Faint aburation; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Ring of protection +1', 'magic', 0, '2000 gp', ['minor', 'ring'], 'This ring offers continual magical protection in the form of a deflection bonus of +1 to +5 to AC. Faint abjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of protection +2', 'magic', 0, '8000 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'This ring offers continual magical protection in the form of a deflection bonus of +1 to +5 to AC. Faint abjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of protection +3', 'magic', 0, '18000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'This ring offers continual magical protection in the form of a deflection bonus of +1 to +5 to AC. Faint abjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of protection +4', 'magic', 0, '32000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring offers continual magical protection in the form of a deflection bonus of +1 to +5 to AC. Faint abjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of protection +5', 'magic', 0, '50000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring offers continual magical protection in the form of a deflection bonus of +1 to +5 to AC. Faint abjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of ram', 'magic', 0, '8600 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'This ornate iron ring bears a ram’s head. On command it spends 1 to 3 charges to strike one target with a ramlike force, a ranged attack out to 50 feet with no range penalty, dealing 1d6 damage per charge; a target within 30 feet is also bull rushed (Strength 25, Large, +1 for 2 charges, +2 for 3). It can also open doors as a character with Strength 25, 27 or 29 (1, 2 or 3 charges). A new ring has 50 charges and is nonmagical once they are gone. Moderate transmutation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Ring of regeneration', 'magic', 0, '90000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This white gold ring continually allows a living wearer to heal 1 point of damage per level every hour rather than every day. (This ability cannot be aided by the Heal skill.) Nonlethal damage heals at a rate of 1 point of damage per level every 5 minutes. If the wearer loses a limb, an organ, or any other body part while wearing this ring, the ring regenerates it as the spell. In either case, only damage taken while wearing the ring is regenerated. Strong conjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Ring of shooting stars', 'magic', 0, '50000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'At night under the open sky, or in shadow or darkness, the ring casts dancing lights once an hour and light twice a night, and has two special powers. Ball lightning, once a night: one to four 3-foot balls, controlled like dancing lights (range 120 feet, speed 120 feet, 4 rounds), that discharge into a creature coming within 5 feet, dealing 4d6 for one ball, 3d6 each for two, 2d6 each for three or 1d6 each for four. Shooting stars, three a week: each flies 70 feet in a straight line, dealing 12 points on impact and 24 fire damage in a 5-foot spread (DC 13 Reflex avoids the impact and halves the fire). Indoors at night or underground, it casts faerie fire twice a day and once a day a spark shower, a 20-foot arc 10 feet wide dealing 2d8 damage, or 4d8 to those wearing metal armor or holding metal weapons. Strong evocation; CL 12th.'],
    ['Ring of spell storing', 'magic', 0, '50000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'As the minor ring of spell storing, except it holds up to five levels of spells. Moderate evocation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Ring of spell storing, major', 'magic', 0, '200000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'As the minor ring of spell storing, except it holds up to ten levels of spells. Strong evocation; CL 17th.'],
    ['Ring of spell storing, minor', 'magic', 0, '18000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'This ring holds up to three levels of spells, which the wearer can cast at the minimum caster level, with no material component, focus or XP cost and no arcane spell failure; activation takes the spell’s casting time (at least a standard action). A spellcaster can cast any spells into it (metamagic versions count at their adjusted level), or use a scroll to put one in, and the ring tells the wearer what it holds. A random ring’s spells are rolled as for a scroll, and it needn’t be full. Faint evocation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of spell turning', 'magic', 0, '98280 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'Up to three times per day on command, this simple platinum band automatically reflects the next nine levels of spells cast at the wearer, exactly as if spell turning had been cast upon the wearer. Strong abjuration; CL 13th.'],
    ['Ring of sustenance', 'magic', 0, '2500 gp', ['minor', 'ring'], 'This ring continually provides its wearer with life-sustaining nourishment. The ring also refreshes the body and mind, so that its wearer needs only sleep 2 hours per day to gain the benefit of 8 hours of sleep. The ring must be worn for a full week before it begins to work. If it is removed, the owner must wear it for another week to reattune it to himself. Faint conjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Ring of swimming', 'magic', 0, '2500 gp', ['minor', 'ring'], 'This silver ring has a wave pattern etched into the band. It continually grants the wearer a +5 competence bonus on Swim checks. Faint transmutation; CL 2nd.'],
    ['Ring of swimming, improved', 'magic', 0, '10000 gp', ['medium', 'ring'], 'As swimming, except it grants a +10 competence bonus on its wearer’s Swim checks. Moderate transmutation; CL 7th.'],
    ['Ring of telekinesis', 'magic', 0, '75000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring allows the caster to use the spell telekinesis on command. Moderate transmutation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Ring of three wishes', 'magic', 0, '97950 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This ring is set with three rubies. Each ruby stores a wish spell, activated by the ring. When a wish is used, that ruby disappears. For a randomly generated ring, roll 1d3 to determine the remaining number of rubies. When all the wishes are used, the ring becomes a nonmagical item. Strong evocation (if miracle is used); CL 20th.'],
    ['Ring of water walking', 'magic', 0, '15000 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'ring'], 'This ring, set with an opal, allows the wearer to continually utilize the effects of the spell water walk. Moderate transmutation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Ring of wizardry I', 'magic', 0, '20000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'This special ring comes in four kinds (ring of wizardry I, ring of wizardry II, ring of wizardry III, and ring of wizardry IV), all of them useful only to arcane spellcasters. The wearer’s arcane spells per day are doubled for one specific spell level. A ring of wizardry I doubles 1st-level spells, a ring of wizardry II doubles 2nd-level spells, a ring of wizardry III doubles 3rd-level spells, and a ring of wizardry IV doubles 4th-level spells. Bonus spells from high ability scores or school specialization are not doubled. Moderate (wizardry I) or strong (wizardry II-IV) (no school); CL 11th (I), 14th (II), 17th (III), 20th (IV).'],
    ['Ring of wizardry II', 'magic', 0, '40000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This special ring comes in four kinds (ring of wizardry I, ring of wizardry II, ring of wizardry III, and ring of wizardry IV), all of them useful only to arcane spellcasters. The wearer’s arcane spells per day are doubled for one specific spell level. A ring of wizardry I doubles 1st-level spells, a ring of wizardry II doubles 2nd-level spells, a ring of wizardry III doubles 3rd-level spells, and a ring of wizardry IV doubles 4th-level spells. Bonus spells from high ability scores or school specialization are not doubled. Moderate (wizardry I) or strong (wizardry II-IV) (no school); CL 11th (I), 14th (II), 17th (III), 20th (IV).'],
    ['Ring of wizardry III', 'magic', 0, '70000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This special ring comes in four kinds (ring of wizardry I, ring of wizardry II, ring of wizardry III, and ring of wizardry IV), all of them useful only to arcane spellcasters. The wearer’s arcane spells per day are doubled for one specific spell level. A ring of wizardry I doubles 1st-level spells, a ring of wizardry II doubles 2nd-level spells, a ring of wizardry III doubles 3rd-level spells, and a ring of wizardry IV doubles 4th-level spells. Bonus spells from high ability scores or school specialization are not doubled. Moderate (wizardry I) or strong (wizardry II-IV) (no school); CL 11th (I), 14th (II), 17th (III), 20th (IV).'],
    ['Ring of wizardry IV', 'magic', 0, '100000 gp', ['major', 'ring'], 'This special ring comes in four kinds (ring of wizardry I, ring of wizardry II, ring of wizardry III, and ring of wizardry IV), all of them useful only to arcane spellcasters. The wearer’s arcane spells per day are doubled for one specific spell level. A ring of wizardry I doubles 1st-level spells, a ring of wizardry II doubles 2nd-level spells, a ring of wizardry III doubles 3rd-level spells, and a ring of wizardry IV doubles 4th-level spells. Bonus spells from high ability scores or school specialization are not doubled. Moderate (wizardry I) or strong (wizardry II-IV) (no school); CL 11th (I), 14th (II), 17th (III), 20th (IV).'],
    ['Ring of x-ray vision', 'magic', 0, '25000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'ring'], 'On command, this ring gives its possessor the ability to see into and through solid matter. Vision range is 20 feet, with the viewer seeing as if he were looking at something in normal light even if there is no illumination. X-ray vision can penetrate 1 foot of stone, 1 inch of common metal, or up to 3 feet of wood or dirt. Thicker substances or a thin sheet of lead blocks the vision. Using the ring is physically exhausting, causing the wearer 1 point of Constitution damage per minute after the first 10 minutes of use in a single day. Moderate divination; CL 6th.'],
    ['Robe of blending', 'magic', 1, '30000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'When this robe is put on, the wearer intuitively knows that the garment has very special properties. A robe of blending enables its wearer to appear to be part of his surroundings. This allows him a +10 competence bonus on Hide checks. The wearer can adopt the appearance of another creature, as with the disguise self spell, at will. All creatures acquainted with and friendly to the wearer see him normally. Moderate illusion; CL 10th.'],
    ['Robe of bones', 'magic', 1, '2400 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This handy item functions much like a robe of useful items for the serious necromancer. It appears to be an unremarkable robe, but a character who dons it notes that it is adorned with small embroidered figures representing undead creatures. Only the wearer of the robe can see the embroidery and recognize them for the creatures they become, and detach them. One figure can be detached each round. Detaching a figure causes it to become an actual undead creature (see the list below). The skeleton or zombie is not under the control of the wearer of the robe, but may be subsequently commanded, rebuked, turned, or destroyed. A newly created robe of bones always has two embroidered figures of each of the following undead: small goblin skeleton; medium human commoner skeleton; medium wolf skeleton; small goblin zombie; medium human commoner zombie; medium wolf zombie. Moderate necromancy [evil]; CL 6th.'],
    ['Robe of eyes', 'magic', 1, '120000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This valuable garment appears to be a normal robe until it is put on. Its wearer is able to see in all directions at the same moment due to scores of visible, magical eyelike patterns that adorn the robe. She also gains 120-foot darkvision. The robe of eyes sees all forms of invisible or ethereal things within 120 feet. The wearer of a robe of eyes gains a +10 competence bonus on Search checks and Spot checks. She retains her Dexterity bonus to AC even when flat-footed, and she can’t be flanked. However, she is not able to avert her eyes or close her eyes when confronted by a creature with a gaze attack. A light or continual flame spell cast directly on a robe of eyes causes it to be blinded for 1d3 minutes. A daylight spell blinds it for 2d4 minutes. Moderate divination; CL 11th.'],
    ['Robe of scintillating colors', 'magic', 1, '27000 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'A full round after its command word, this robe flows with dazzling colors, for up to 10 rounds a day in all. They act as a gaze attack out to 30 feet: those who look at the wearer are dazed for 1d4+1 rounds (Will DC 16 negates; a mind-affecting pattern). Attacks against the wearer have a 10 percent miss chance, rising by 10 percent each round to 50 percent. The robe lights a 30-foot radius. Moderate illusion; CL 11th.'],
    ['Robe of stars', 'magic', 1, '58000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This garment is typically black or dark blue and embroidered with small white or silver stars. The robe has three magical powers. It enables its wearer to travel physically to the Astral Plane, along with all that she is wearing or carrying; it gives its wearer a +1 luck bonus on all saving throws; its wearer can use up to six of the embroidered stars on the chest portion of the robe as +5 shuriken. The robe grants its wearer proficiency with such weapons. Each shuriken disappears after it is used. Strong varied; CL 15th.'],
    ['Robe of the archmagi', 'magic', 1, '75000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This normal-appearing garment can be white (01-45 on d%, good alignment), gray (46-75, neither good nor evil alignment), or black (76-100, evil alignment). Its wearer, if an arcane spellcaster, gains the following powers. +5 armor bonus to AC; spell resistance 18; +4 resistance bonus on all saving throws; +2 enhancement bonus on caster level checks made to overcome spell resistance. If a white robe is donned by an evil character, she immediately gains three negative levels. The reverse is true with respect to a black robe donned by a good character. An evil or good character who puts on a gray robe, or a neutral character who dons either a white or black robe, gains two negative levels. While these negative levels never result in lost levels, they remain as long as the garment is worn and cannot be overcome in any way (including restoration spells). Strong varied; CL 14th.'],
    ['Robe of useful items', 'magic', 1, '7000 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'Only the wearer of this plain robe sees its cloth patches, and can detach one a round to turn it into a real item. A new robe has two each of: dagger, bullseye lantern (filled and lit), steel mirror, 10-foot pole, 50-foot hempen rope, and sack. It also has 4d4 other patches (d%): a bag of 100 gp, a 500 gp silver coffer, an iron door that fits an opening, 10 gems worth 100 gp each, a 24-foot ladder, a mule with saddlebags, a 10-foot pit, a potion of cure serious wounds, a 12-foot rowboat, a minor scroll of one random spell, a pair of war dogs, a window, or a portable ram. A removed patch can’t be replaced. Moderate transmutation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Rod of absorption', 'magic', 5, '50000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'Held in hand, this rod draws in single-target spells or rays aimed at you or your gear, with no action needed, nullifying them and storing their levels, which you learn as it absorbs them. You can spend stored levels to cast spells you have prepared (without using the preparation) or, as a bard or sorcerer, spells you know, of a level up to what is stored, providing any material components. It absorbs fifty spell levels in all, can’t be recharged, and you know how much it can still absorb and holds. A found rod has d% ÷ 2 levels of potential left, and on another d% roll of 71–100 still holds half of the levels already absorbed. Strong abjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Rod of alertness', 'magic', 5, '85000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'This rod looks like a +1 light mace with eight flanges, and is one. It gives a +1 insight bonus on initiative. Grasped firmly, it casts detect chaos, evil, good, law or magic, discern lies, light or see invisibility (each a standard action). Once a day, planted in the ground and willed to alertness (a standard action), it senses any creature within 120 feet that intends to harm you, casts prayer on allies within 20 feet and warns them, for 10 minutes. Once a day, planted, it animates up to eleven Small objects around it for 11 rounds, as animate objects. Moderate abjuration, divination, enchantment, and evocation; CL 11th.'],
    ['Rod of cancellation', 'magic', 5, '11000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'rod'], 'This dreaded rod is a bane to magic items, for its touch drains an item of all magical properties. The item touched must make a DC 23 Will save to prevent the rod from draining it. If a creature is holding it at the time, then the item can use the holder’s Will save bonus in place of its own if the holder’s is better. In such cases, contact is made by making a melee touch attack roll. Upon draining an item, the rod itself becomes brittle and cannot be used again. Drained items are only restorable by wish or miracle. (If a sphere of annihilation and a rod of cancellation negate each other, nothing can restore either of them.) Strong abjuration; CL 17th.'],
    ['Rod of enemy detection', 'magic', 5, '23500 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'This device pulses in the wielder’s hand and points in the direction of any creature or creatures hostile to the bearer of the device (nearest ones first). These creatures can be invisible, ethereal, hidden, disguised, or in plain sight. Detection range is 60 feet. If the bearer of the rod concentrates for a full round, the rod pinpoints the location of the nearest enemy and indicates how many enemies are within range. The rod can be used three times each day, each use lasting up to 10 minutes. Activating the rod is a standard action. Moderate divination; CL 10th.'],
    ['Rod of flailing', 'magic', 5, '50000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'Upon the command of its possessor, the rod activates, changing from a normal-seeming rod to a +3 dire flail. The dire flail is a double weapon, which means that each of the weapon’s heads can be used to attack. The wielder can gain an extra attack (with the second head) at the cost of making all attacks at a -2 penalty (as if she had the Two-Weapon Fighting feat). Once per day the wielder can use a free action to cause the rod to grant her a +4 deflection bonus to Armor Class and a +4 resistance bonus on saving throws for 10 minutes. The rod need not be in weapon form to grant this benefit. Transforming it into a weapon or back into a rod is a move action. Moderate enchantment; CL 9th.'],
    ['Rod of flame extinguishing', 'magic', 5, '15000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'rod'], 'A touch (a standard action) puts out a Medium or smaller nonmagical fire. One charge puts out a Large or larger nonmagical fire or a Medium or smaller magic fire, and suppresses continual magic flames for 6 rounds; 2 charges put out a Large or larger magic fire such as fireball or wall of fire. With a readied action inside its area, it counters an instantaneous fire spell. Against a fire creature, a melee touch attack and 3 charges deal 6d6 damage. It has 10 charges, renewed every day. Strong transmutation; CL 12th.'],
    ['Rod of lordly might', 'magic', 10, '70000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'This heavy metal rod with a flanged ball and six buttons weighs 10 pounds. Once a day each: hold person on a touch (Will DC 14); fear on enemies within 10 feet who see it (Will DC 16 partial); and a touch dealing 2d4 damage (Will DC 17 half) that cures you as much. At will, it is a +2 light mace, or, by button: 1, a +1 flaming longsword; 2, a +4 battleaxe; 3, a +3 shortspear or longspear up to 15 feet long, usable as a lance; 4, a climbing pole of 5 to 50 feet that anchors in granite and bears 4,000 pounds (5 retracts it), which can also force open doors with a +12 Strength modifier; 6, pointing to magnetic north and telling your depth or height. Pushing a button is like drawing a weapon. Strong enchantment, evocation, necromancy, and transmutation; CL 19th.'],
    ['Rod of metal and mineral detection', 'magic', 5, '10500 gp', ['medium', 'rod'], 'This rod pulses in the wielder’s hand and points to the largest mass of metal within 30 feet. However, the wielder can concentrate on a specific metal or mineral. If the specific mineral is within 30 feet, the rod points to any places it is located, and the rod wielder knows the approximate quantity as well. If more than one deposit of the specified metal or mineral is within range, the rod points to the largest cache first. Each operation requires a full-round action. Moderate divination; CL 9th.'],
    ['Rod of negation', 'magic', 5, '37000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'This device negates the spell or spell-like function or functions of magic items. The wielder points the rod at the magic item, and a pale gray beam shoots forth to touch the target device, attacking as a ray (a ranged touch attack). The ray functions as a greater dispel magic spell, except it only affects magic items. To negate instantaneous effects from an item, the rod wielder needs to have used a ready action. The dispel check uses the rod’s caster level (15th). The target item gets no saving throw, although the rod can’t negate artifacts (even minor artifacts). The rod can function three times per day. Strong varied; CL 15th.'],
    ['Rod of python', 'magic', 10, '13000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'rod'], 'This rod is longer than normal rods. It is about 4 feet long and weighs 10 pounds. It strikes as a +1/+1 quarterstaff. If the user throws the rod to the ground (a standard action), it grows to become a giant constrictor snake by the end of the round. The python obeys all commands of the owner. (In animal form, it retains the +1 enhancement bonus on attacks and damage possessed by the rod form.) The serpent returns to rod form (a full-round action) whenever the wielder desires, or whenever it moves farther than 100 feet from the owner. If the snake form is slain, it returns to rod form and cannot be activated again for three days. A python rod only functions if the possessor is good. Moderate transmutation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Rod of rulership', 'magic', 5, '60000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'This rod looks like a royal scepter worth at least 5,000 gp in materials and workmanship alone. The wielder can command the obedience and fealty of creatures within 120 feet when she activates the device (a standard action). Creatures totaling 300 Hit Dice can be ruled, but creatures with Intelligence scores of 12 or higher are entitled to a DC 16 Will save to negate the effect. Ruled creatures obey the wielder as if she were their absolute sovereign. Still, if the wielder gives a command that is contrary to the nature of the creatures commanded, the magic is broken. The rod can be used for 500 total minutes before crumbling to dust. This duration need not be continuous. Strong enchantment; CL 20th.'],
    ['Rod of security', 'magic', 5, '61000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'Activating this rod (a standard action) takes you and every creature touching it, or linked hand in hand, to a nondimensional pocket paradise; unwilling creatures get a DC 17 Will save. Up to 200 creatures can stay 200 days divided by their number (rounded down). There, creatures don’t age, heal naturally at twice the normal rate, and have fresh water, fruit and vegetables in a comfortable climate. When it ends or you dismiss it, everyone reappears where they were, shifted aside if the space is taken. It can be activated once a week. Strong conjuuration; CL 20th.'],
    ['Rod of splendor', 'magic', 5, '25000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'While you hold or carry it, you gain a +4 enhancement bonus to Charisma. Once a day it garbs you in noble clothing, furs and jewels worth 1d4+6 × 1,000 gp for 12 hours; all of it vanishes if any part is sold, given away, used as a component or taken from you. Once a week, on command, it raises a silk pavilion 60 feet across with furnishings and food to entertain up to a hundred people, lasting one day; everything from it, even what was carried out, then disappears. Strong conjuration and transmutation; CL 12th.'],
    ['Rod of thunder and lightning', 'magic', 5, '33000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'This iron rod with silver rivets is a +2 light mace. Once a day each, as free actions: thunder, striking as a +3 light mace and stunning the target (Fortitude DC 16 negates); and lightning, adding 2d6 electricity damage to a hit, or to a miss that would still hit as a touch attack. Once a day each, as standard actions: thunderclap, as shout (Fortitude DC 16 partial, 2d6 sonic, deafened 2d6 rounds); and lightning stroke, a 5-foot bolt to 200 feet for 9d6 electricity (Reflex DC 16 half). Once a week: thunder and lightning, both at once, the bolt’s dice counting 1s and 2s as 3s and the thunderclap hitting everything within 10 feet of it, with one DC 16 Reflex save for both. Moderate evocation; CL 9th.'],
    ['Rod of viper', 'magic', 5, '19000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'rod'], 'This rod strikes as a +2 heavy mace. Once per day, upon command, the head of the rod becomes that of an actual serpent for 10 minutes. During this period, any successful strike with the rod deals its usual damage and also poisons the creature hit. The poison deals 1d10 points of Constitution damage immediately (Fortitude DC 14 negates) and another 1d10 points of Constitution damage 1 minute later (Fortitude DC 14 negates). The rod only functions if its possessor is evil. Moderate necromancy; CL 10th.'],
    ['Rod of withering', 'magic', 5, '25000 gp', ['major', 'rod'], 'A rod of withering acts as a +1 light mace that deals no hit point damage. Instead, the wielder deals 1d4 points of Strength damage and 1d4 points of Constitution damage to any creature she touches with the rod (by making a melee touch attack). If she scores a critical hit, the damage from that hit is permanent ability drain. In either case, the defender negates the effect with a DC 17 Fortitude save. Strong necromancy; CL 13th.'],
    ['Rod of wonder', 'magic', 5, '12000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'rod'], 'Activating this unpredictable rod is a standard action, and each use rolls a random effect (d%), such as: slow on the target (Will DC 15); faerie fire; deluding you for a round about what it did; a windstorm-force gust of wind; reading surface thoughts; stinking cloud; heavy rain; summoning a rhino, elephant or mouse; a 6d6 lightning bolt or fireball (Reflex DC 15 half); 600 blinding butterflies; enlarge person; darkness; grass growing; turning an object ethereal; shrinking you to 1/12 height; making you invisible; leaves growing from the target; a stream of 1 gp gems dealing 1 damage each; blinding colors (Fortitude DC 15); turning you or the target permanently blue, green or purple; or flesh to stone (Fortitude DC 18). Moderate enchantment; CL 10th.'],
    ['Rope of climbing', 'magic', 3, '3000 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'A 60-foot-long rope of climbing is no thicker than a wand, but it is strong enough to support 3,000 pounds. Upon command, the rope snakes forward, upward, downward, or in any other direction at 10 feet per round, attaching itself securely wherever its owner desires. It can unfasten itself and return in the same manner. A rope of climbing can be commanded to knot or unknot itself. This causes large knots to appear at 1-foot intervals along the rope. Knotting shortens the rope to a 50-foot length until the knots are untied but lowers the DC of Climb checks while using it by 10. A creature must hold one end of the rope when its magic is invoked. Faint transmutation; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Rope of entanglement', 'magic', 5, '21000 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'A rope of entanglement looks just like any other hempen rope about 30 feet long. Upon command, the rope lashes forward 20 feet or upward 10 feet to entangle a victim. An entangled creature can break free with a DC 20 Strength check or a DC 20 Escape Artist check. The rope has AC 22, 12 hit points, and hardness 10, and it has damage reduction 5/slashing as well. The rope repairs damage to itself at a rate of 1 point per 5 minutes, but if a rope of entanglement is severed (all 12 hit points lost to damage), it is destroyed. Moderate transmutation; CL 12th.'],
    ['Salve of slipperiness', 'magic', 0, '1000 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This substance provides a +20 competence bonus on all Escape Artist checks, meaning that it is almost impossible to grapple such a character or to tie or chain him up. In addition, such obstructions as webs (magical or otherwise) do not affect an anointed individual. Magic ropes and the like do not avail against this salve. If it is smeared on a floor or on steps, the area should be treated as a long-lasting grease spell. The salve requires 8 hours to wear off normally, or it can be wiped off with an alcohol solution (even wine). Salve of slipperiness is needed to coat the inside of a container that is meant to hold sovereign glue (see below). Faint conjuration; CL 6th.'],
    ['Scabbard of keen edges', 'magic', 1, '16000 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This scabbard is fashioned from cured leather and fine silver. It can shrink or enlarge to accommodate any knife, dagger, sword, or similar weapon up to and including a greatsword. Up to three times per day on command, the scabbard casts keen edge on any blade placed within it. Faint transmutation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Scarab of protection', 'magic', 0, '38000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This device appears to be a silver medallion in the shape of a beetle. If it is held for 1 round, an inscription appears on its surface letting the holder know that it is a protective device. The scarab’s possessor gains spell resistance 20. The scarab can also absorb energy-draining attacks, death effects, and negative energy effects. Upon absorbing twelve such attacks, the scarab turns to powder and is destroyed. Strong abjuration and necromancy; CL 18th.'],
    ['Scarab, golembane', 'magic', 0, '2500 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This beetle-shaped pin enables its wearer to detect any golem within 60 feet, although he must concentrate (a standard action) in order for the detection to take place. A scarab enables its possessor to combat golems with weapons, unarmed attacks, or natural weapons as if those golems had no damage reduction. Moderate divination; CL 8th.'],
    ['Screaming bolt', 'magic', 0, '267 gp', ['minor', 'weapon'], 'One of these +2 bolts screams when fired, forcing all enemies of the wielder within 20 feet of the path of the bolt to succeed on a DC 14 Will save or become shaken. This is a mind-affecting fear effect. Faint enchantment; CL 5th.'],
    ['Scroll, 0-level spell', 'magic', 0, '12 gp 5 sp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 0-level spell written at caster level 1st, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 1st-level spell', 'magic', 0, '25 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 1st-level spell written at caster level 1st, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 2nd-level spell', 'magic', 0, '150 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 2nd-level spell written at caster level 3rd, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 3rd-level spell', 'magic', 0, '375 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 3rd-level spell written at caster level 5th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 4th-level spell', 'magic', 0, '700 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 4th-level spell written at caster level 7th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 5th-level spell', 'magic', 0, '1125 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 5th-level spell written at caster level 9th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 6th-level spell', 'magic', 0, '1650 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 6th-level spell written at caster level 11th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 7th-level spell', 'magic', 0, '2275 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 7th-level spell written at caster level 13th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 8th-level spell', 'magic', 0, '3000 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 8th-level spell written at caster level 15th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Scroll, 9th-level spell', 'magic', 0, '3825 gp', ['scroll'], 'One arcane or divine 9th-level spell written at caster level 17th, the lowest for a wizard or cleric (a spell with a costly material component or XP cost costs more). Reading it is a spell completion activation: the spell must be on your class list and you need the ability score to cast it (10 + its level), but not the caster level; if your caster level is lower than the scroll’s, you must succeed on a caster level check (DC scroll’s caster level + 1). Arcane and divine scrolls work only for their own kind of caster. Reading it uses the scroll up.'],
    ['Shatterspike', 'magic', 4, '4315 gp', ['medium', 'weapon'], 'Wielders without the Improved Sunder feat use Shatterspike as a +1 longsword only; wielders with the Improved Sunder feat add a +4 bonus (including the sword’s +1 enhancement bonus) to the opposed roll when attempting to strike a foe’s weapon. If successful, Shatterspike deals 1d8+4 points of damage plus the wielder’s Strength modifier to the target weapon (the target weapon’s hardness must still be overcome with each hit). Shatterspike can damage weapons with an enhancement bonus of +4 or lower. Strong evocation; CL 13th.'],
    ['Shield, +1', 'magic', 0, '1150 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'shield'], 'A +1 enhancement bonus to the shield’s bonus to AC. The price includes the 150 gp for masterwork shield; add the base shield’s cost. Faint abjuration; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Shield, +2', 'magic', 0, '4150 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'shield'], 'A +2 enhancement bonus to the shield’s bonus to AC. The price includes the 150 gp for masterwork shield; add the base shield’s cost. Moderate abjuration; CL 6th.'],
    ['Shield, +3', 'magic', 0, '9150 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'shield'], 'A +3 enhancement bonus to the shield’s bonus to AC. The price includes the 150 gp for masterwork shield; add the base shield’s cost. Moderate abjuration; CL 9th.'],
    ['Shield, +4', 'magic', 0, '16150 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'shield'], 'A +4 enhancement bonus to the shield’s bonus to AC. The price includes the 150 gp for masterwork shield; add the base shield’s cost. Strong abjuration; CL 12th.'],
    ['Shield, +5', 'magic', 0, '25150 gp', ['major', 'shield'], 'A +5 enhancement bonus to the shield’s bonus to AC. The price includes the 150 gp for masterwork shield; add the base shield’s cost. Strong abjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Shifter’s sorrow', 'magic', 10, '12780 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'weapon'], 'This +1/+1 two-bladed sword has blades of alchemical silver. The weapon deals an extra 2d6 points of damage against any creature with the shapechanger subtype. When a shapechanger or a creature in an alternate form (such as a druid using wild shape) is struck by the weapon, it must make a DC 15 Will save or return to its natural form. Strong transmutation; CL 15th.'],
    ['Silver dagger, masterwork', 'magic', 0, '322 gp', ['minor', 'weapon'], 'This masterwork alchemical silver dagger is nonmagical. As a masterwork weapon, it has a +1 enhancement bonus on attack rolls. No aura (nonmagical).'],
    ['Silversheen', 'magic', 0, '250 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This substance can be applied to a weapon as a standard action. It will give the weapon the properties of alchemical silver for 1 hour, replacing the properties of any other special material it might have. One vial will coat a single melee weapon or 20 units of ammunition. Faint transmutation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Slaying arrow', 'magic', 0, '2282 gp', ['medium', 'minor', 'weapon'], 'This +1 arrow is keyed to one type or subtype of creature (d%: 01-05 aberrations, 06-09 animals, 10-16 constructs, 17-22 dragons, 23-27 elementals, 28-32 fey, 33-39 giants, 40 aquatic humanoids, 41-42 dwarves, 43-44 elves, 45 gnolls, 46 gnomes, 47-49 goblinoids, 50 halflings, 51-54 humans, 55-57 reptilian humanoids, 58-60 orcs, 61-65 magical beasts, 66-70 monstrous humanoids, 71-72 oozes, 73 air outsiders, 74-76 chaotic outsiders, 77 earth outsiders, 78-80 evil outsiders, 81 fire outsiders, 82-84 good outsiders, 85-87 lawful outsiders, 88 water outsiders, 89-90 plants, 91-98 undead, 99-100 vermin). If it strikes such a creature, the target must make a DC 20 Fortitude save or die (or, if unliving, be destroyed) instantly; even creatures normally exempt from Fortitude saves, such as undead and constructs, are subject to it. Against a living creature this is a death effect, so death ward protects the target. Strong necromancy; CL 13th.'],
    ['Slaying arrow (greater)', 'magic', 0, '4057 gp', ['medium', 'weapon'], 'This +1 arrow is keyed to one type or subtype of creature (d%: 01-05 aberrations, 06-09 animals, 10-16 constructs, 17-22 dragons, 23-27 elementals, 28-32 fey, 33-39 giants, 40 aquatic humanoids, 41-42 dwarves, 43-44 elves, 45 gnolls, 46 gnomes, 47-49 goblinoids, 50 halflings, 51-54 humans, 55-57 reptilian humanoids, 58-60 orcs, 61-65 magical beasts, 66-70 monstrous humanoids, 71-72 oozes, 73 air outsiders, 74-76 chaotic outsiders, 77 earth outsiders, 78-80 evil outsiders, 81 fire outsiders, 82-84 good outsiders, 85-87 lawful outsiders, 88 water outsiders, 89-90 plants, 91-98 undead, 99-100 vermin). If it strikes such a creature, the target must make a DC 23 Fortitude save or die (or, if unliving, be destroyed) instantly; even creatures normally exempt from Fortitude saves, such as undead and constructs, are subject to it. Against a living creature this is a death effect, so death ward protects the target. Strong necromancy; CL 13th.'],
    ['Sleep arrow', 'magic', 0, '132 gp', ['minor', 'weapon'], 'This +1 arrow is painted white and has white fletching. If it strikes a foe so that it would normally deal damage, it instead bursts into magical energy that deals nonlethal damage (in the same amount as would be lethal damage) and forces the target to make a DC 11 Will save or fall asleep. Faint enchantment; CL 5th.'],
    ['Slippers of spider climbing', 'magic', 0.5, '4800 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'When worn, a pair of these slippers enable movement on vertical surfaces or even upside down along ceilings, leaving the wearer’s hands free. Her speed is 20 feet. Severely slippery surfaces—icy, oiled, or greased surfaces— make these slippers useless. The slippers can be used for 10 minutes per day, split up as the wearer chooses. Faint transmutation; CL 4th.'],
    ['Sovereign glue', 'magic', 0, '2400 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This thick amber adhesive can only be kept in a flask lined with an ounce of salve of slipperiness, renewed within a round each time glue is poured out. A flask found holds 1d8−1 ounces (minimum 1). An ounce covers 1 square foot and bonds virtually any two substances permanently. It sets in 1 round; pulled apart before then (a move action), that application is wasted. Once set, only universal solvent separates the bond. Strong transmutation; CL 20th.'],
    ['Spined shield', 'magic', 0, '5580 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'shield'], 'This +1 heavy steel shield is covered in spines. It acts as a normal spiked shield. On command up to three times per day, the shield’s wearer can fire one of the shield’s spines. A fired spine has a +1 enhancement bonus, a range increment of 120 feet, and deals 1d10 points of damage (19-20/x2). Fired spines regenerate each day. Moderate evocation; CL 6th.'],
    ['Staff of abjuration', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'Usually carved from the heartwood of an ancient oak or other large tree, this staff allows use of the following spells: shield (1 charge); resist energy (1 charge); dispel magic (1 charge); lesser globe of invulnerability (2 charges); dismissal (2 charges); repulsion (3 charges). Strong abjuration; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of charming', 'magic', 5, '16500 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'Made of twisting wood ornately shaped and carved, this staff allows use of the following spells: charm person (1 charge); charm monster (2 charges). Moderate enchantment; CL 8th.'],
    ['Staff of conjuration', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This staff is usually made of ash or walnut and bears ornate carvings of many different kinds of creatures. It allows use of the following spells: unseen servant (1 charge); summon swarm (1 charge); stinking cloud (1 charge); minor creation (2 charges); cloudkill (2 charges); summon monster VI (3 charges). Strong conjuration; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of defense', 'magic', 5, '58250 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'The staff of defense is a simple-looking staff that throbs with power when held defensively. It allows use of the following spells: shield (1 charge); shield of faith (1 charge); shield other (1 charge); shield of law (3 charges). Strong abjuration; CL 15th.'],
    ['Staff of divination', 'magic', 5, '73500 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'Made from a supple length of willow, often with a forked tip, this staff allows use of the following spells: detect secret doors (1 charge); locate object (1 charge); tongues (1 charge); locate creature (2 charges); prying eyes (2 charges); true seeing (3 charges). Strong divination; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of earth and stone', 'magic', 5, '80500 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This staff is topped with a fist-sized emerald that gleams with smoldering power. It allows the use of the following spells: passwall (1 charge); move earth (1 charge). Moderate transmutation; CL 11th.'],
    ['Staff of enchantment', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'Often made from applewood and topped with a clear crystal, this staff allows use of the following spells: sleep (1 charge); hideous laughter (1 charge); suggestion (1 charge); crushing despair (2 charges); mind fog (2 charges); suggestion, mass (3 charges). Strong enchantment; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of evocation', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'Usually very smooth and carved from hickory, willow, or yew, this staff allows use of the following spells: magic missile (1 charge); shatter (1 charge); fireball (1 charge); ice storm (2 charges); wall of force (2 charges); chain lightning (3 charges). Strong evocation; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of fire', 'magic', 5, '17750 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'Crafted from bronzewood with brass bindings, this staff allows use of the following spells: burning hands (1 charge); fireball (1 charge); wall of fire (2 charges). Moderate evocation; CL 8th.'],
    ['Staff of frost', 'magic', 5, '56250 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'Tipped on either end with a glistening diamond, this rune-covered staff allows use of the following spells: ice storm (1 charge); wall of ice (1 charge); cone of cold (2 charge). Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Staff of healing', 'magic', 5, '27750 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'This white ash staff, with inlaid silver runes, allows use of the following spells: lesser restoration (1 charge); cure serious wounds (1 charge); remove blindness/deafness (2 charges); remove disease (3 charges). Moderate conjuration; CL 8th.'],
    ['Staff of illumination', 'magic', 5, '48250 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'This staff is usually sheathed in silver and decorated with sunbursts. It allows use of the following spells: dancing lights (1 charge); flare (1 charge); daylight (2 charges); sunburst (3 charges). Strong evocation; CL 15th.'],
    ['Staff of illusion', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This staff is made from ebony or other dark wood and carved into an intricately twisted, fluted, or spiral shape. It allows use of the following spells: disguise self (1 charge); mirror image (1 charge); major image (1 charge); rainbow pattern (2 charges); persistent image (2 charges); mislead (3 charges). Strong illusion; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of life', 'magic', 5, '155750 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'Made of thick oak shod in gold, this staff allows use of the following spells: heal (1 charge); raise dead (5 charges). Moderate conjuration; CL 11th.'],
    ['Staff of necromancy', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This staff is made from ebony or other dark wood and carved with the images of bones and skulls. It allows use of the following spells: cause fear (1 charge); ghoul touch (1 charge); halt undead (1 charge); enervation (2 charges); waves of fatigue (2 charges); circle of death (3 charges). Strong necromancy; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of passage', 'magic', 5, '170500 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This potent item allows use of the following spells: dimension door (1 charge); passwall (1 charge); phase door (2 charges); greater teleport (2 charges); astral projection (2 charges). Strong varied; CL 17th.'],
    ['Staff of power', 'magic', 5, '211000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This +2 quarterstaff gives its wielder a +2 luck bonus to AC and saves, and for 1 charge (a free action) deals double damage (×3 on a critical) for a round. Spells, 1 charge: magic missile, ray of enfeeblement, lightning bolt and fireball (each heightened to 5th level), continual flame, levitate; 2 charges: cone of cold, hold monster, wall of force (a 10-foot hemisphere around you), globe of invulnerability. Retributive strike: break it (a standard action if deliberate) to release every charge in a 30-foot radius: 8 × charges damage within 2 squares, 6 × within 4, 4 × within 6 (Reflex DC 17 half). You have a 50 percent chance of escaping to another plane, or are destroyed. With no charges left, it remains a +2 quarterstaff. Strong varied; CL 15th.'],
    ['Staff of size alteration', 'magic', 5, '29000 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'Stout and sturdy, this staff of dark wood allows use of the following spells: enlarge person (1 charge); reduce person (1 charge); shrink item (1 charge); enlarge person, mass (1 charge); reduce person, mass (1 charge). Faint conjuration; CL 8th.'],
    ['Staff of swarming insects', 'magic', 5, '24750 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'staff'], 'Made of twisted dark wood with dark spots resembling crawling insects (which occasionally seem to move), this staff allows use of the following spells: summon swarm (1 charge); insect plague (3 charges). Moderate conjuration; CL 9th.'],
    ['Staff of transmutation', 'magic', 5, '65000 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'This staff is generally carved from or decorated with petrified wood and allows use of the following spells: expeditious retreat (1 charge); alter self (1 charge); blink (1 charge); polymorph (2 charges); baleful polymorph (2 charges); disintegrate (3 charges). Strong transmutation; CL 13th.'],
    ['Staff of woodlands', 'magic', 5, '101250 gp', ['major', 'staff'], 'Appearing to have grown naturally into its shape, this oak, ash, or yew staff allows use of the following spells: charm animal (1 charge); speak with animals (1 charge); barkskin (2 charges); wall of thorns (3 charges); summon nature’s ally VI (3 charges); animate plants (4 charges). The staff may be used as a weapon, functioning as a +2 quarterstaff. The staff of the woodlands also allows its wielder to pass without trace at will, with no charge cost. These two attributes continue to function after all the charges are expended. Moderate varied; CL 13th.'],
    ['Stone horse, courser', 'magic', 6000, '10000 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This item has the statistics of a heavy warhorse as well as having hardness 10. Strong transmutation; CL 14th.'],
    ['Stone horse, destrier', 'magic', 6000, '14800 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This item has the statistics of a heavy warhorse as well as having hardness 10. Strong transmutation; CL 14th.'],
    ['Stone of alarm', 'magic', 2, '2700 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This stone cube, when given the command word, affixes itself to any object. If that object is touched thereafter by anyone who does not first speak that same command word, the stone emits a piercing screech for 1 hour that can be heard up to a quarter-mile away (assuming no intervening barriers). Faint abjuration; CL 3rd.'],
    ['Stone of controlling earth elementals', 'magic', 5, '100000 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'A stone of this nature is typically an oddly shaped bit of roughly polished rock. The possessor of such a stone need but utter a few words of summoning, and a Huge earth elemental comes to the summoner. The summoning words require 1 full round to speak, and in all ways the stone functions as the summon monster VII spell. (If sand or rough, unhewn stone is the summoning medium, the elemental that comes is Large instead, and the stone functions as the summon monster VI spell.) The elemental appears in 1d4 rounds. Only one elemental can be summoned at a time. A new elemental requires a new patch of earth or stone, which cannot be accessed until after the first elemental disappears (is dispelled, dismissed, or slain). Strong conjuration; CL 13th.'],
    ['Stone of good luck (luckstone)', 'magic', 0, '20000 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This stone is typically a bit of rough polished agate or some similar mineral. Its possessor gains a +1 luck bonus on saving throws, ability checks, and skill checks. Faint evocation; CL 5th.'],
    ['Stone salve', 'magic', 0, '4000 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This ointment has two uses. If an ounce of it is applied to the flesh of a petrified creature, it returns the creature to flesh as the stone to flesh spell. If an ounce of it is applied to the flesh of a nonpetrified creature, it protects the creature as a stoneskin spell. Strong abjuration and transmutation; CL 13th.'],
    ['Strand of prayer beads', 'magic', 0, '25800 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This seems a normal string of prayer beads until its owner casts a divine spell, revealing its powers. It has a bead of healing, a bead of karma and a bead of smiting. Blessing casts bless; healing, cure serious wounds, remove blindness/deafness or remove disease; karma gives +4 caster level for 10 minutes; smiting, chaos hammer, holy smite, order’s wrath or unholy blight (Will DC 17 partial); summons calls a powerful creature of your alignment from the Outer Planes to aid you for a day (summoning a deity’s emissary frivolously brings a geas and the loss of your items); wind walking casts wind walk. Each bead works once a day, summons only once ever, and a bead removed loses its power. Blessing, smiting and wind walking are spell trigger items; karma and summons work for any divine caster. The strand just has to be carried. Faint, moderate or strong (many schools); CL 1st (blessing), 5th (healing), 7th (smiting), 9th (karma), 11th (wind walking), 17th (summons).'],
    ['Strand of prayer beads, greater', 'magic', 0, '95800 gp', ['major', 'wondrous'], 'This seems a normal string of prayer beads until its owner casts a divine spell, revealing its powers. It has a bead of healing, a bead of karma, a bead of summons and a bead of wind walking. Blessing casts bless; healing, cure serious wounds, remove blindness/deafness or remove disease; karma gives +4 caster level for 10 minutes; smiting, chaos hammer, holy smite, order’s wrath or unholy blight (Will DC 17 partial); summons calls a powerful creature of your alignment from the Outer Planes to aid you for a day (summoning a deity’s emissary frivolously brings a geas and the loss of your items); wind walking casts wind walk. Each bead works once a day, summons only once ever, and a bead removed loses its power. Blessing, smiting and wind walking are spell trigger items; karma and summons work for any divine caster. The strand just has to be carried. Faint, moderate or strong (many schools); CL 1st (blessing), 5th (healing), 7th (smiting), 9th (karma), 11th (wind walking), 17th (summons).'],
    ['Strand of prayer beads, lesser', 'magic', 0, '9600 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This seems a normal string of prayer beads until its owner casts a divine spell, revealing its powers. It has a bead of blessing and a bead of healing. Blessing casts bless; healing, cure serious wounds, remove blindness/deafness or remove disease; karma gives +4 caster level for 10 minutes; smiting, chaos hammer, holy smite, order’s wrath or unholy blight (Will DC 17 partial); summons calls a powerful creature of your alignment from the Outer Planes to aid you for a day (summoning a deity’s emissary frivolously brings a geas and the loss of your items); wind walking casts wind walk. Each bead works once a day, summons only once ever, and a bead removed loses its power. Blessing, smiting and wind walking are spell trigger items; karma and summons work for any divine caster. The strand just has to be carried. Faint, moderate or strong (many schools); CL 1st (blessing), 5th (healing), 7th (smiting), 9th (karma), 11th (wind walking), 17th (summons).'],
    ['Sun blade', 'magic', 0, '50335 gp', ['major', 'weapon'], 'This sword looks like a bastard sword and deals its damage, but is wielded as a short sword in weight and ease, and proficiency or Weapon Focus with either applies (not stacking). It is a +2 bastard sword, +4 against evil creatures, and deals double damage (×3 on a critical) to undead and Negative Energy Plane creatures. Once a day, swung overhead with a command word, it sheds radiance like full daylight, spreading from 10 feet by 5 feet a round for 10 rounds to a 60-foot radius, fading a minute after you stop. It is good: an evil creature wielding it gains a negative level while it is in hand, never causing actual level loss. Moderate evocation; CL 10th.'],
    ['Sustaining spoon', 'magic', 0, '5400 gp', ['minor', 'wondrous'], 'This unremarkable eating utensil is typically fashioned from horn. If the spoon is placed in an empty container the vessel fills with a thick, pasty gruel. Although this substance has a flavor similar to that of warm, wet cardboard, it is highly nourishing and contains everything necessary to sustain any herbivorous, omnivorous, or carnivorous creature. The spoon can produce sufficient gruel each day to feed up to four humans. Faint conjuration; CL 5th.'],
    ['Sword of life stealing', 'magic', 0, '25715 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'weapon'], 'This black iron +2 longsword bestows a negative level when it deals a critical hit. The sword wielder gains 1d6 temporary hit points each time a negative level is bestowed on another. These temporary hit points last for 24 hours. One day after being struck, subjects must make a DC 16 Fortitude save for each negative level or lose a character level. Strong necromancy; CL 17th.'],
    ['Sword of subtlety', 'magic', 0, '22310 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'weapon'], 'A +1 short sword with a thin, dull gray blade, this weapon provides a +4 bonus on its wielder’s attack and damage rolls when he is making a sneak attack with it. Moderate illusion; CL 7th.'],
    ['Sword of the planes', 'magic', 0, '22315 gp', ['major', 'medium', 'weapon'], 'This longsword has an enhancement bonus of +1 on the Material Plane, but on any Elemental Plane its enhancement bonus increases to +2. (The +2 enhancement bonus also applies on the Material Plane when the weapon is used against elementals.) It operates as a +3 longsword on the Astral Plane or the Ethereal Plane or when used against opponents native to either of those planes. On any other plane, or against any outsider, it functions as a +4 longsword. Strong evocation; CL 15th.'],
    ['Sylvan scimitar', 'magic', 0, '47315 gp', ['major', 'weapon'], 'This +3 scimitar, when used outdoors in a temperate climate, grants its wielder the use of the Cleave feat and deals an extra 1d6 points of damage. Moderate evocation; CL 11th.'],
    ['Tome of clear thought +1', 'magic', 5, '27500 gp', ['medium', 'wondrous'], 'This heavy book contains instruction on improving memory and logic, but entwined within the words is a powerful magical effect. If anyone reads this book, which takes a total of 48 hours over a minimum of six days, she gains an inherent bonus of from +1 to +5 (depending on the type of tome) to her Intelligence score. Once the book is read, the magic disappears from the pages and it becomes a normal book. Because the tome of clear thought provides an inherent bonus, the reader will earn extra skill points when she attains a new level. Strong evocation (if miracle is used); CL 17th.'],
